{"id":"src/lib/live/kolkataStore.ts","pkg":"src/lib/live","kind":"module","lines":177,"commentLines":14,"header":["THE SAVED TRAINS OF THE KOLKATA TERMINALS (Howrah, Sealdah, Santragachi, Kolkata) THAT GO OVER NEITHER DURGAPUR NOR ASANSOL, with their fares (src/lib/live/kolkataSet.ts says which trains these are). Three tables, closed to the public roles like the other fare tables (src/lib/nl2sql/sql/32_train_kol.sql): public.train_kol the CATALOGUE: one row for every train that STARTS at one of the four stations, whether it is in the set or not (in_set, and the reason when it is out), with its details and its halts with times; public.train_fare_kol the fare of each class from the starting station to the END of the run, one row per train (the same shape as train_fare, with from_code because the starting station differs); public.train_fare_leg_kol the fare to EVERY halt after the starting station, one row per train and halt (the same shape as train_fare_leg). Everything has the time it was received. The fares are the railway's reservation system's own, through RailRadar's paid fare service (to 14 Dec 2026). Nothing here is personal data. I made these tables of their own, and did not widen FareStation (fareStore.ts), so that nothing about the Durgapur and Asansol tabs can change."],"symbols":[{"name":"Queryable","kind":"interface","exported":true,"line":14,"generics":"","extends":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"method","name":"query","line":15,"sig":"query(sql: string, params?: unknown[]): Promise<any>;","params":[{"name":"sql","type":"string","optional":false,"rest":false,"def":""},{"name":"params","type":"unknown[]","optional":true,"rest":false,"def":""}],"returns":"Promise<any>","doc":[]}],"id":"9e88b28d9c-Queryable","usedBy":[]},{"name":"KOL_TABLES","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":18,"sig":"const KOL_TABLES = { trains: \"train_kol\", fares: \"train_fare_kol\", legs: \"train_fare_leg_kol\" } as const","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"9e88b28d